= Conclusion

In this experiment, we calibrated the spectrometer and tried to identify an unknown source. By comparing the measured wavelengths with the literature values, we were able to identify most of the characteristic spectral lines of mercury. We are therefore fairly certain that the unknown source was mercury.

Furthermore, we analyzed the solar spectrum and were able to identify several Fraunhofer lines, although not all of them. One of the main difficulties was that the spectrum was recorded using several overlapping images. Since these images had different intensities, combining them into a single consistent spectrum was challenging. As a result, we tried to analyze them separately.

Despite the difficulties, we were able to demonstrate how the spectral lines can be looked at as fingerprints and has been proven to be a useful tool to identify different sources.

For future experiments the result could be improved py ensuring more consistent conditions  between each picture or longer exposure times to average out fluctuations.


